      "message": "Please update this as `# SURS test change -- DO NOT COMMIT`\nOtherwise, the CI will *always fail*.\n\nContext: https://github.com/FDio/vpp/actions/runs/32187246224/\nPython requires every `from __future__ import ...` statement to appear *before* any executable statement other than the module docstring, comments, and blank lines.\nThis is what you have now:\n```\n\"\"\"BFD tests\"\"\"\n\n\"\"\" SURS test change -- DO NOT COMMIT \"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import division\n```\n*Only the first string literal can count as the module docstring*. The second one is treated as a regular Python statement, so the future import is no longer at the beginning of the file.\nThat is why all `make test` in the CI are failing with `SyntaxError: from __future__ imports must occur at the beginning of the file`.",
